I walk past a small stall.
It smells of fresh bread.
I walk over to the stall.
The baker is standing behind a large table.
The table is full of baked goods.
I see a dark rye bread.
It looks very fresh.
I point at the rye bread.
"How much does the dark rye bread cost?" I ask.
The baker wipes his hands.
"It costs thirty-five kroner," he replies.
"I am buying it," I say.
I take out my payment card.
I pay with the card.
The baker gives me the bread in a paper bag.
I touch the bag.
The bread is still warm.
I look forward to eating it.
